obs Draft row for the ledger, held here until headroom exists: REDS %840 (20261010.152007) -- tally kumara sign() panics on a mismatched keypair. What went wrong: sign() wraps Ed25519 sign in catch unreachable, and a KeyPair assembled from mismatched parts reaches the panic (metal probe: panic attempt to unwrap error KeyMismatch, exit 134). What caught it: the 70-line and catch-unreachable census over mantra/ and tally/. What it taught: a safe-looking unreachable on a fallible std call is an assert in disguise only when the input cannot be built wrong. Status: OPEN, the additive sign_checked door is GREEN (fda5a4b03e), the legacy sign() awaits the seam ruling on amphora, aurora and comlink callers.
